<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sa die de sa Sardigna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1794">1794</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Sardinia Day</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sa die de sa Sardigna ('<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a>'s Day') is the regional holiday of Sardinia, held on 28 April. It commemorates the uprising of 28 April 1794 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cagliari">Cagliari</a>, when the people drove out the Piedmontese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> and officials after the court in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin">Turin</a> rejected the island's demands for a share in government. It was made an official regional day in 1993.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sa-die-de-sa-sardigna.jpg" alt="Sa die de sa Sardigna" width="320" height="163" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giuseppe Sciuti · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ingresso_a_Sassari.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
